            <ArticleTitle>CT-guided biopsy in two cases of retroperitoneal fibrosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>230-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.clinimag.2008.02.021</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diffuse retroperitoneal fibrosis (RPF) is a rare inflammatory process. We report on two known cases of RPF, without evidence of involvement of the urinary tract or of the venous system. A computed tomography (CT)-guided biopsy was performed in each case, and the histological findings eliminated other pathological processes, particularly those of malignant origin. In both cases, a therapy with cortisone was instituted, and a follow-up with CT at 6 months has demonstrated a regression of the pathology of more than 50%.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
